Export cedarc's decoded frames as dmabuf

CedarC's decoders allocate their own frames and hand out an 88 byte
descriptor per output buffer, holding the frame's dmabuf fd. Reuse the
upstream dmabuf export path (so far Zynq only) for it: the output pool
wraps a dup of that fd, so frames go downstream without a copy. The copy
fallback without our pool reads the frame through the descriptor. The
frames are padded (720p is 736 lines), the caps take the visible size from
the output crop. CPU consumers map a frame once rather than once per plane,
each dmabuf map syncs the whole frame.
Selected with the cedarc-dmabuf-output hack, only in CedarC's default
buffer mode.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor specific]

